      "id": "claim_ed9eae03961d435ead3b4a8821a9ab20",
      "statement": "Rules 600 and 610 are internal underwriting controls: Rule 100 prohibits using the Manual to alter coverage, and Rule 600 makes inspection evidence part of risk selection and file handling rather than stating a premium, deductible, settlement, or coverage result.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://manuals/underwriting/manual.md#L13-L37",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3d49e53083a482d727f10c22844a715d4ebd216e331a9bd013d016fdd337687e:"
