      "id": "claim_8fc8ee050c30475eaaa59a892c2b2d38",
      "statement": "State and product overlays impose distinct inspection and evidence controls: California requires an acceptable roof inspection before binding at 20 years or greater and retains inspection, photograph, and repair evidence, Florida requires inspection at 15 years or greater and prohibits binding at 20 years or greater with a wind-mitigation inspection above $500,000 Coverage A, and North Carolina requires inspection at 18 years or greater with a wind-mitigation inspection above $500,000 Coverage A; Florida OIR-2023-04 separately requires reliable age and condition evidence and a retained record for roof-age underwriting and adverse action.",
